{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists","id":19994,"title":"Mortal Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T17:56:26-08:00","id":19994,"title":"Mortal Antagonists","content":"I get the weirdest inspiration sometimes. I was playing Arkham Origins and then it hit me: Use some sci-fi to have mortal humans do battle with Scions.<br /> <br /> I know that Scion is supposed to be modern fantasy but I like to mix things up some to keep the players guessing. It keeps the game refreshing for me and also for my players since they have no idea what I will toss at them next.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for what kind of tech/tactics can be used to combat Epic Social/Mental Knacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T18:44:08-08:00","id":20007,"title":"","content":"This depends on what Legend your Scions are. After Legend 5 or so, mortals just stand absolutely <i>zero chance</i> of hurting a Scion. Once they're applying +7 auto-successes to their rolls, Scions just don't care much about getting shot by a tank or whatever mortals can throw at them. Hero-level Scions, however, are not as lucky. They can massively out-class mortals, but in big groups or with heavy combat equipment (like tanks), mortals do stand a decent chance of hurting a Hero.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to get some weird sci-fi technology involved, then that works. Just have it basically apply Epics to the mortals, or give them psychic powers to mimic supernatural abilities, or whatever. Scifi tech is basically ST's choice because there are no rules for it. You have to make up what it does anyway, so just have it do whatever you want to challenge your Scions with. Just remember they could get their hands on it, and if it provides such nice bonuses for mortals, it'll be utter bonkers in the hands of a Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T18:50:44-08:00","id":20010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=20007#post20007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This depends on what Legend your Scions are. After Legend 5 or so, mortals just stand absolutely <i>zero chance</i> of hurting a Scion. Once they're applying +7 auto-successes to their rolls, Scions just don't care much about getting shot by a tank or whatever mortals can throw at them. Hero-level Scions, however, are not as lucky. They can massively out-class mortals, but in big groups or with heavy combat equipment (like tanks), mortals do stand a decent chance of hurting a Hero.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to get some weird sci-fi technology involved, then that works. Just have it basically apply Epics to the mortals, or give them psychic powers to mimic supernatural abilities, or whatever. Scifi tech is basically ST's choice because there are no rules for it. You have to make up what it does anyway, so just have it do whatever you want to challenge your Scions with. Just remember they could get their hands on it, and if it provides such nice bonuses for mortals, it'll be utter bonkers in the hands of a Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make an item or empowerment that provides more power the weaker you are though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:05:05-08:00","id":20012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists#post19994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the weirdest inspiration sometimes. I was playing Arkham Origins and then it hit me: Use some sci-fi to have mortal humans do battle with Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just screams \u201cTrinity Continuum crossover\u201d. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T21:06:32-08:00","id":20069,"title":"","content":"Telgar, I am not talking tanks. But they could use things like sonar to help with anything blinding. They can use certain compounds to fend off fear. So forth and so on. We are not talking Aeon level tech. Nor are we talking about things as simple as guns. I have a story idea but, unfortunately my players cruise the forums so I can't go into full detail about it but will gladly message anyone who wants to know more about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T01:37:51-08:00","id":20135,"title":"","content":"If you are using RAW then mortals are exactly as dangerous as the Storyteller wants them to be. <b>Hero Page 180</b> gives you access to Full Teamwork and Limited Teamwork, which can be applied to a wide range of actions. You could declare that a large mob of mortals provide limited teamwork on their mental resistance roll because of mob mentality. You could declare that a nationwide manhunt for the scions provide limited teamwork on their investigation or survival rolls to find the band. You could declare that a hundred archers are providing limited teamwork on their archery attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Since you are the Storyteller, you decide when mortals become 'redundant'.</b> You could decide that every 10 mortals adds +1 limited teamwork, or every 100 mortals adds +1 limited teamwork, or even every 1000 mortals adds +1 limited teamwork. The rule gives you ultimate flexibility for making mortals dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=KeTBqolcrO8#t=30\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=KeTBqolcrO8#t=30\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=KeTBqolcrO8#t=30\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=KeTBqolcrO8#t=30 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":".  More dramatic second in the video. 11-29-2013, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T09:26:39-08:00","id":20218,"title":"","content":"I've thought a lot about running a scion campaign in a setting that's closer to Shadowrun. I'd basically just let mortals have limited access to boons via magic and knack/epics via cybernetics. Nothing's fleshed out, but if you're just making NPCs it doesn't have to be unless you're the type that shows the players what they were up against after it's all over (which I am). For PCs nothing change except the flavor, so while one PC might have super strength because his dad is Thor, another has it because his dad is president of Globodyne Cybernetics and he lost his meat arm in a horrible paperclip accident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:07:25-08:00","id":20283,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds me of &quot;Skinner&quot; from Werewolf the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T16:41:12-08:00","id":20430,"title":"","content":"Just a suggestion, but you could do something akin to Supernatural, where the mortals manage to get their hands on an item from the mythology that is supposed to be effective against gods from that pantheon. Then it would be a matter of them managing to wound the Hero / Demigod / God with said item. Granted some items may be extremely difficult to get their hands on, but if they're not the best humanity has to offer, they probably weren't going to win anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T23:51:33-08:00","id":20522,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions guys. I am combining these into multiple ideas and they are really great ones. The lightness of setting material means that it is a tabula rasa on which we can imprint any ideas we wish. I am taking advantage of that to make my own enemies for the party beyond the things that they might be aware of such as hydras and manticores and dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T12:41:29-08:00","id":20730,"title":"","content":"I may be of a little bit different opinion, but I feel like humans can be threats to Scions up to pretty high Demigod. It just is a question of what tools said humans are using. At legend 2-4, normal &quot;small arms&quot; type weapons are going to be effective to various extents, especially if you have well-trained adversaries who use intelligent tactics. Legend 5 and 6 means that your Scions can probably deal with tank hits and whatnot, and that's the kind of adversary to send against them. higher legend probably would require multiple cruise missile strikes, but could still do damage to a Scion, or at least that's how I'd run it. I haven't statted up nukes, but they'd be presumably effective as well. Of course, that would require the Scions to piss off nuclear-capable Nation-States.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T18:13:29-08:00","id":20900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=20730#post20730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Of course, that would require the Scions to piss off nuclear-capable Nation-States.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't met my players. Their characters could do it without even trying...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T12:25:31-08:00","id":21247,"title":"","content":"I may have done this in an incredibly dumb way yesterday, but I started trying to think about nuke damage in the context of other weapons that have already been written up. As the highest-damage melee weapon in Core, I chose the Labrys as my unit (8L).<br /> <br /> Now, before trying to scale these things, it's necessary to make particular assumptions. There are three ways that damage dice could scale: roughly linearly, where as you increase the destructiveness you increase the dice by a roughly equal amount (twice as destructive is twice as many dice), roughly logarithmically, where as you increase in destructiveness dice increase but gradually level off, and roughly exponentially, where if you, say, double the destructiveness you'd roll four times as many dice.<br /> <br /> I assume that dice should scale linearly, even though some things in Scion (eg epics) don't. And please note that all these figures are ballpark, and yield figures, where relevant, are sourced from wikipedia which tends to be relatively reliable on such things. I'm totally down for people to critique my numbers, because I did these up on a train yesterday and they may not be totally accurate<br /> <br /> Mk 84 Standard bomb (yield roughly 1 ton of TNT &quot;T&quot;, the standard unit of explosive yield): roughly 10 labrys, for on the order of 80 dice of damage, averaging to around 40 levels of lethal damage<br /> <br /> Tomahawk cruise missile (2T): twice a Mk84, for 160 dice or 80 levels on average<br /> <br /> now that you've seen my scaling for explosives, let's go nuclear. <br /> Little Boy (Hiroshima bomb): 16,000T<br /> Mk 83 (common US fusion weapon): 1,600,000<br /> Tsar Bomba (largest fusion weapon ever detonated): 58,000,000T<br /> <br /> So even if you say that one ton of TNT does only one die of lethal, if you nuke your players with a Mk 83, you roll 1.6 million dice, for an average of 800,000 damage. <br /> <br /> And the only core knack that'd let you soak that is Skin Shedding. There isn't anything else I can think of that comes even remotely close to that. You need an Exalted-style perfect dodge or perfect soak.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T14:05:17-08:00","id":21283,"title":"","content":"Why are you all trying to have mortals match your Scions blow-for-blow?<br /> <br /> It's not an accident that the most diabolical foes of flying brick superheroes tend to be &quot;normals&quot; who are just exceptionally clever.<br /> <br /> Mortals should be about putting Scions into compromising situations. Locking a Scion in a cage that is specifically designed to negate their powers, for instance.<br /> <br /> Or getting them caught on camera &quot;murdering&quot; a Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Things that are going to present major problems and obstacles for the group without, you know, trying to find ways for armed mortals to be more than wheat before the scythe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T14:29:17-08:00","id":21295,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> If mortals use nukes, what with all that implies, are they going to be good guys?<br /> <br /> I suppose a deity of fire wouldn't be pleased if his scion was attacked by such &quot;puny&quot; weaponry to begin with.<br /> <br /> Sorry, for interjecting here, just rambling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T14:31:37-08:00","id":21298,"title":"","content":"In part I did the writeup I did as an intellectual exercise. And I don't believe that mortals should match scions blow for blow inherently. Mortals who are smart, and who use the tools available to them, which includes armaments but could also be things like getting low-level scions on terrorist watch lists or whatever, should be able to, if not necessarily utterly decimate a large group of scions, then at least present enough of a threat that they cannot be utterly discounted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T14:50:04-08:00","id":21306,"title":"","content":"Mortals that are smarter than scions with dots in &quot;Wits&quot; and &quot;Intelligence&quot; need to be on par with Dr. Doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:07:48-08:00","id":21311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21306#post21306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals that are smarter than scions with dots in &quot;Wits&quot; and &quot;Intelligence&quot; need to be on par with Dr. Doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even necessarily with Wits and Intelligence of exceptional caliber, frankly. A particularly dogged investigator can be far more dangerous than a smarmy professor, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:13:26-08:00","id":21317,"title":"","content":"Dayen, I like your thinking and that was something I was going for. No one to go toe-to-toe with the Scion PC's but more along the lines of how to beat them and to bring them down. To humble them. To capture them. Not to kill them in a fight. Killing off the PC's does nothing to increase their legend unless I want to have a story where they go to the Underworld to rescue their fallen comrade.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I am not afraid to kill them off but I want it to be a major plot point when they die. I think that if a Scion dies, it should not be a bad die roll...or if it is, then it should be a change in the Cycle.<br /> <br /> I wanted to use mortals to harass and endanger the Scions (who are on the cusp of demigodhood but not quite there yet) and to progress the storyline.<br /> <br /> Guitarsniper, I would use the stats from the level 10 power for Industry, The Project, when I want to do a nuke to someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 12-01-2013, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:08:08-08:00","id":21340,"title":"","content":"I think there is absolutely a genre and theme where the idea of mortals as individuals, as organizations, as nations and as a unified race standing up against the eldritch powers of the Gods and saying &quot;<b>NO!</b>&quot; is amazing. It shines a light on the power of human free will, ingenuity and stubbornness to refuse to bow to <i>anything</i>, even the Gods. I can see an amazing series of stories told where Demigods are hounded by the FBI and DHS. Where their power and abilities make them terrifying to normal people and they become Public Enemy Number One. X-Men does a pretty good take on this with the Sentinels and their associated villains. <br /> <br /> In that game of genre, I think humans mobilizing armies and navies, using air strikes, traps, mines, bombs and even nuclear devices to fight back against the power of myth and legend is going to be effective. A Band of cowering Demigods huddled in a bunker trying to ride out the bombardment, praying to their parents for salvation while the fearful humans throw everything they've got against the Other. I can totally see it. The greatest minds in the world trying to do <i>anything</i> to get rid of this supernatural presence in <i>their</i> orderly, mundane world. Humanity has outgrown the Gods and resents their influence and their power. Even the Gods themselves can't match the strength of the united human race, striking against them every time they come to Earth. Only in the Overworld are the Gods safe from human reprisals. Maybe it was even this fear of growing human ingenuity and independence that drove the Gods from the World centuries ago. <br /> <br /> But, that isn't what I think Scion is about. So if a Titanspawn corrupts top US Generals into launching a nuclear strike on the hometown of a Band of Scions while they're resting, then the Guardian of the Group is going to stand strong, throw up a Ward and defend his people against the puny devices of <i>science</i> with the power of his Legend. For me, Scion is a hopeful game and, ultimately, about victory. Not victory over humans, but victory in general. Humanity isn't the center of the story. The PC's are. They're more than human, and it's <i>their</i> time to shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:16:05-08:00","id":21348,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21311#post21311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even necessarily with Wits and Intelligence of exceptional caliber, frankly. A particularly dogged investigator can be far more dangerous than a smarmy professor, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>A character that can &quot;think and react with supernatural speed&quot; among other supernatural traits isn't likely to be particularly perturbed. Add a little &quot;manipulation&quot; however and this investigator can be made useful to the character in question.<br /> Humans...pawns...same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:22:43-08:00","id":21353,"title":"","content":"I agree with you, partially, on your thoughts, Telgar. The main thing is, the gods and Titans and even Scions do indeed bow down to Mortals since it is the Mortal's power to tell the Story that binds the gods to their forms. It is their tale-telling that creates Legends. So Mortals are more powerful than even the gods and Titans when it all comes down to it.<br /> <br /> I do see how the PC's are the most important people in the world but that does not mean that they are the most powerful or the most skilled or the most anything other than important. So the game does revolve around them but that does not mean that they can defeat anyone or anything. There should always be something more powerful than the players so that they have something to rage against.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T17:43:57-08:00","id":21364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21295#post21295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...<br /> <br /> If mortals use nukes, what with all that implies, are they going to be good guys?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another idea to note is not what kind of weapons the mortals can use, but what sort of weapons they will be forced to use. Nuclear strikes are usually a last resort option for most militaries, especially when used on home soil.<br /> <br /> It would be completely absurd to have your mortals say <b>&quot;oooh, a god! Let's nuke him!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I think it would / should only reach such a level of conflict if your characters are the one provoking the attack, such as causing massive levels of destruction across the country. Which may very well lead them to some fate bonds or some such consequences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T17:57:19-08:00","id":21366,"title":"","content":"Scion's kinda vague about how exactly humanity and Fate are related. There's some kind of relation, but it isn't clear what that relationship <i>is</i> or how it works. Still, humanity collectively creating Fate through their expectations and beliefs is a valid reading. In that sense, yes, the collective of Humanity is the greatest power in the setting since they are the force that generates and maintains Fate.<br /> <br /> That said, I think human antagonists work really, really well at Hero and <i>very</i> low Legend Demigod. Up till about Legend 5, maybe 6, humans are indeed a significant threat to Scions. By Legend 7 and certainly Legend 8, Scions can reshape the World however they want. They can forge new nations, create new religions, decimate armies and all kind of crazy stuff like that. It's not that mortal antagonists have <i>no</i> place in Scion, but that place is limited. <br /> <br /> When the correct response to, say, Jormungdar rampaging through Scandinavia is to call in a barrage of ICBMs or tactical nuclear munitions, I feel that Scion has lost something of its focus on mythology and epic adventure. Instead it becomes a game of political influence to control mortal forces and weapons. When the adventuring heroes become an inconvenience getting in the way of the <i>real</i> heroes (the military), I just can't see them as the heroes anymore. It'd be like if instead of fighting to save New York City from the aliens, the Avengers had done the responsible, legal thing and called the Pentagon to scramble fighters, bombers, the National Guard and special forces troops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:07:38-08:00","id":21370,"title":"","content":"Um...I recall that they were going to nuke NYC in that movie.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:09:36-08:00","id":21371,"title":"","content":"And that was the <i>bad</i> solution. Not the <i>good</i> solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:32:25-08:00","id":21385,"title":"","content":"In the end, things like this are always going to depend on the storyteller, and party, in question. If I'm in someone else's game, I'll do my best to respect your views on how the setting works, in pretty much every respect, as I hope they would respect mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T20:13:00-08:00","id":21416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21385#post21385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, things like this are always going to depend on the storyteller, and party, in question. If I'm in someone else's game, I'll do my best to respect your views on how the setting works, in pretty much every respect, as I hope they would respect mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my stance, exactly. The players and the ST are the ones telling the story book be damned. Hence the Golden Rule of all WW games. So if they all decide that suddenly, Scions have powers akin to novas and not Epics/Knacks/Purviews/Boons, then so be it. If they want Scions to be manifestations of the gods and not children of them, then so be it.<br /> <br /> It is the table's ability and right to go &quot;You know what? F*ck this rule/peice of setting. We will do it this way.&quot; and should anyone else jump into the game, then they should understand how things work. That is also a big reason why I am leery of jumping into games since my vision of things may differ from what the players have had happen in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T23:39:43-08:00","id":21472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21364#post21364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Another idea to note is not what kind of weapons the mortals can use, but what sort of weapons they will be forced to use. Nuclear strikes are usually a last resort option for most militaries, especially when used on home soil.<br /> <br /> It would be completely absurd to have your mortals say <b>&quot;oooh, a god! Let's nuke him!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I think it would / should only reach such a level of conflict if your characters are the one provoking the attack, such as causing massive levels of destruction across the country. Which may very well lead them to some fate bonds or some such consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people overestimate the willingness of nuclear powers to utilize their arsenals, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> If a deity were to appear in New York tomorrow I have absolutely no doubt that the U.S. military would prepare to blow it up with missiles within the hour. If so ordered, I have no doubt they would execute that attack.<br /> <br /> But really, getting a bunch of demigods hung up on a murder one wrap is the sort of thing mortals can and should be doing to your heroes if they're being particularly sloppy.<br /> <br /> Jail sucks. Jail is something nobody wants to have to deal with. Even in a tabletop game. Especially in a tabletop game. Even if they make bail they're going to have to surrender their documents, which means from a legal perspective they're stuck wherever they are.<br /> <br /> Of course, by all means, this sort of stratagem isn't reserved for mortal foes, whatever and whomever they are. Certainly a Titan could have mortal followers execute these sorts of machinations to slow down the heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T00:14:25-08:00","id":21478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21472#post21472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people overestimate the willingness of nuclear powers to utilize their arsenals, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> If a deity were to appear in New York tomorrow I have absolutely no doubt that the U.S. military would prepare to blow it up with missiles within the hour. If so ordered, I have no doubt they would execute that attack.<br /> <br /> But really, getting a bunch of demigods hung up on a murder one wrap is the sort of thing mortals can and should be doing to your heroes if they're being particularly sloppy.<br /> <br /> Jail sucks. Jail is something nobody wants to have to deal with. Even in a tabletop game. Especially in a tabletop game. Even if they make bail they're going to have to surrender their documents, which means from a legal perspective they're stuck wherever they are.<br /> <br /> Of course, by all means, this sort of stratagem isn't reserved for mortal foes, whatever and whomever they are. Certainly a Titan could have mortal followers execute these sorts of machinations to slow down the heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've gotta stop telling my players the kinds of things I may or may not throw at them :P<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, you're right: clued-in humans won't try to fight Scions, they'll try to hit them from other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T01:08:00-08:00","id":21486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21472#post21472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people overestimate the willingness of nuclear powers to utilize their arsenals, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> If a deity were to appear in New York tomorrow I have absolutely no doubt that the U.S. military would prepare to blow it up with missiles within the hour. If so ordered, I have no doubt they would execute that attack.<br /> <br /> But really, getting a bunch of demigods hung up on a murder one wrap is the sort of thing mortals can and should be doing to your heroes if they're being particularly sloppy.<br /> <br /> Jail sucks. Jail is something nobody wants to have to deal with. Even in a tabletop game. Especially in a tabletop game. Even if they make bail they're going to have to surrender their documents, which means from a legal perspective they're stuck wherever they are.<br /> <br /> Of course, by all means, this sort of stratagem isn't reserved for mortal foes, whatever and whomever they are. Certainly a Titan could have mortal followers execute these sorts of machinations to slow down the heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not saying they wouldn't nuke them, I'm saying the ST should have a justified action for them doing so. If it's just a god brawling a Titan Spawn in the middle of the street, I would think blowing up the city as a first response is going to be a PR nightmare. Now if that god had been causing Class 5 tornadoes or 300 yard tall Tsunamis, or city destroying earthquakes, then yes, that would probably be a justified response.<br /> <br /> Unless the realization that there are actual god-like beings walking around causes the government to go bat shit crazy in an attempt to control the situation, I think they would have better reserved judgement on how to deal with the crisis at hand, if any at all. That's why I think a better alternative would be to have mortals (highly trained ones) use weaponry from the mythos that is supposed to be effective on the gods. If I remember correctly, the blood of a Hind (may not be spelling that correctly) was supposed to be a lethal poison to the Greek gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T05:31:39-08:00","id":21569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21472#post21472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people overestimate the willingness of nuclear powers to utilize their arsenals, but that's neither here nor there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree there.<br /> ~~Unless we're talking India and Pakistan...(Yeah, the real world is a bit crazier than we thought)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21472#post21472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a deity were to appear in New York tomorrow I have absolutely no doubt that the U.S. military would prepare to blow it up with missiles within the hour. If so ordered, I have no doubt they would execute that attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree. Unless you're speaking of your own game.<br /> I don't think NY would believe it's a god. They'd be more likely to believe it was an alien.<br /> A non-nuclear strike is still more of an option. Any president authorizing the use of nuclear weapons on US soil isn't going to president much longer unless we're talking a proven imminent national threat.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21472#post21472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jail sucks. Jail is something nobody wants to have to deal with. Even in a tabletop game. Especially in a tabletop game. Even if they make bail they're going to have to surrender their documents, which means from a legal perspective they're stuck wherever they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! Just sitting around for days on end doesn't make for a good game. Unless the characters in question are meant to be delayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T06:06:20-08:00","id":21580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21486#post21486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I think a better alternative would be to have mortals (highly trained ones) use weaponry from the mythos that is supposed to be effective on the gods. If I remember correctly, the blood of a Hind (may not be spelling that correctly) was supposed to be a lethal poison to the Greek gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you have me wondering about some kind of mortal run SCP/MiB organization.<br /> <br /> They know gods are real, they know Scions exist. They know about Titans and most of their job is studying and containing Titanspawns. And the occasional dangerous Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:57:37-08:00","id":21671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21569#post21569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree there.<br /> ~~Unless we're talking India and Pakistan...(Yeah, the real world is a bit crazier than we thought)</div> </div> </div> </div>Having dealt with members of both countries' military I do not wish to re-evaluate my opinion regarding the willingness of nuclear powers to utilize their arsenal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21569#post21569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagree. Unless you're speaking of your own game.<br /> I don't think NY would believe it's a god. They'd be more likely to believe it was an alien.<br /> A non-nuclear strike is still more of an option. Any president authorizing the use of nuclear weapons on US soil isn't going to president much longer unless we're talking a proven imminent national threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err, yes, I suppose I should have been more clear. They'd start with a cruise missile in my estimation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21569#post21569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep! Just sitting around for days on end doesn't make for a good game. Unless the characters in question are meant to be delayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why in your game, in this one instance, they will get their bail hearing in exactly 24 hours. Hopefully they'll have the lawyer problem sorted out.<br /> <br /> But the entire point is to hassle, delay, and hamper their efforts to &quot;be themselves,&quot; which is something players instinctively dislike. I mean, they could also break out of jail, but that's probably the end of the campaign at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:39:39-08:00","id":21709,"title":"","content":"Unless they just use their Charisma, Manipulation or Appearance to convince the arresting officers that these aren't the Demigods they're looking for. Then they don't go to jail. And they pick up a phone and call the President of the USA and God's Honest him into believing they're innocent, so that he pardons them. <br /> <br /> Dealing with mortal authorities shortly becomes child's play for well-developed Scions much past Hero. Because at the end of the day, the people you're dealing with are human and humans can't beat or even come close to your level of ability and power. If you want them to declare you innocent, or make you a law-exempt officially-license vigilante, you can have them do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:01:13-08:00","id":21732,"title":"","content":"Telgar has the right of it. Mortals are ultimately glass cannons. There are rules in place that allow you to make mortals <b>INCREDIBLY</b> lethal and dangerous to Scions, but at the same time they crumble like a house of cards beneath the offensive efforts of any Scion.<br /> <br /> The mortals would have to be seriously organized to imprison even Legend 2 heroes for any prolonged length of time. The biggest difference will be whether or not a large organization of mortals knows about Scions and have taken appropriate measures, and that is a setting question every storyteller decides for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:57:27-08:00","id":21766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21732#post21732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telgar has the right of it. Mortals are ultimately glass cannons. There are rules in place that allow you to make mortals <b>INCREDIBLY</b> lethal and dangerous to Scions, but at the same time they crumble like a house of cards beneath the offensive efforts of any Scion.<br /> <br /> The mortals would have to be seriously organized to imprison even Legend 2 heroes for any prolonged length of time. The biggest difference will be whether or not a large organization of mortals knows about Scions and have taken appropriate measures, and that is a setting question every storyteller decides for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary stumbling block for Scions is their own inattentiveness. Sure, you can convince Officer Schmoe to let you walk out of jail. But did you track down Judge Funk and convince him to scrub your records and destroy court documents?<br /> <br /> This is the sort of problem, indeed an actual paper trail (digital though it may be in places) that can really ruin a Scion's day. Nothing says irritating like cops showing up to arrest you while you're at your day job, or trying to convince someone to help you, or similarly compromised.<br /> <br /> Obviously a large organization (or organizations) who prioritize tripping up Scions would be more effective at it, but that's not to say that the average accrual of legal detritus cannot bring a significant amount of pain to even a demigod. Particularly ones who want to continue to make their way in the mortal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:21:27-08:00","id":21783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21766#post21766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several good points.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly a player issue, not a character issue. Your average Wits or Intelligence Scion is going to figure out the majority of the paper trail and be able to take actions to eliminate it. Players do not have the Wits or Intelligence of their characters and often overlook these details. Also, few players want to spend their limited game time hunting down and eliminating said paper trail.<br /> <br /> But in spite of everything I just said, missing important details is a staple of many mythological tales. So everything you said are all very good and relevant plot elements!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T12:06:03-08:00","id":21812,"title":"","content":"Let's say a Scion does find himself arrested. He still gets a trial. He puts the mind-whammy on the judge and instantaneously get's the case dismissed. Let's say it's a jury trial. He puts the mind-whammy on enough people to get him into the jury chambers and mind-whammies them into believing he's innocent. If he can't get to the jury himself, one of his Bandmates can probably pull it off.<br /> <br /> Now let's say a Scion actually goes to jail. He mind-whammies EVERYONE in the prison into becoming his bitches. Instantaneously, he's the king of his own little empire. Even if he doesn't escape, he'll be quite comfortable.<br /> <br /> Then there's the small matter of the Fateful Aura. Fate doesn't WANT Scions sitting on their assess doing nothing. So, the Scion decides to remain in prison. Before long a freaking DRAGON attacks the prison trying to get at him. He can sit back and watch the whole prison die (and likely die himself) or he can fight the dragon and probably wreck half the prison in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T14:01:58-08:00","id":21878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21812#post21812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say a Scion does find himself arrested. He still gets a trial. He puts the mind-whammy on the judge and instantaneously get's the case dismissed. Let's say it's a jury trial. He puts the mind-whammy on enough people to get him into the jury chambers and mind-whammies them into believing he's innocent. If he can't get to the jury himself, one of his Bandmates can probably pull it off.<br /> <br /> Now let's say a Scion actually goes to jail. He mind-whammies EVERYONE in the prison into becoming his bitches. Instantaneously, he's the king of his own little empire. Even if he doesn't escape, he'll be quite comfortable.<br /> <br /> Then there's the small matter of the Fateful Aura. Fate doesn't WANT Scions sitting on their assess doing nothing. So, the Scion decides to remain in prison. Before long a freaking DRAGON attacks the prison trying to get at him. He can sit back and watch the whole prison die (and likely die himself) or he can fight the dragon and probably wreck half the prison in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which end up creating more problems for the Scion in the end when they don't properly clean up after themselves.<br /> <br /> I absolutely am not suggesting you frequently entangle your players in legal red tape, but as a once-in-a-while reminder that there's a world trying to go about its business out there it's probably going to be a refreshing change of pace. Certainly, there's not a whole lot of challenge in running around bending mortals' wills to do your bidding, but there is a lot of time and effort involved in getting to everyone you need to.<br /> <br /> I've used these sorts of &quot;FLIPPING MORTAL BULL!&quot; sessions to force players to re-assess their current activities. No real preference on how the players exit the situation, but a reminder that just because you're a superpowerful being who can say &quot;get me $100 from your bank account&quot; <i>and get it</i> doesn't mean you should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T14:06:40-08:00","id":21880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21878#post21878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of which end up creating more problems for the Scion in the end when they don't properly clean up after themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the first two options I put forward. If the judge dismisses the case, that's it. Your criminal record's clear. Jury finds you innocent? No harm no foul. Sure law enforcement might start keeping an eye on you, but they can't move against you again until they have evidence that you're a suspect in some other crime. Even the &quot;take over the prison&quot; thing isn't a big problem for you. No one's going to report anything you do. The guards and the Warden are in your pocket too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T14:30:34-08:00","id":21890,"title":"","content":"One of the fun parts about Scion appears to be the lack of any sort of Masquerade system. If your Scions are put in danger, by mortal authorities, they could pull out this card:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you see the monsters running around? You see the natural disasters springing up all over the place? I'm trying to put a STOP to that, and without me, you would all fucking die by the end of the week! How about you let me do my job?&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted it may not work all the time, but some of the more intelligent mortals may take it into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:02:54-08:00","id":21955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21880#post21880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not the first two options I put forward. If the judge dismisses the case, that's it. Your criminal record's clear. Jury finds you innocent? No harm no foul. Sure law enforcement might start keeping an eye on you, but they can't move against you again until they have evidence that you're a suspect in some other crime. Even the &quot;take over the prison&quot; thing isn't a big problem for you. No one's going to report anything you do. The guards and the Warden are in your pocket too.</div> </div> </div> </div>as long as you have the Legend to burn to put, and keep, everyone you need in your pocket. That's the nice thing about having a &quot;currency&quot; that regenerates more slowly than, say, Essence in Exalted: being out of, or low on, legend and willpower can make things significantly difficult for you. Sure, some knacks don't cost Legend to activate, but many do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:18:48-08:00","id":21964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21955#post21955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as long as you have the Legend to burn to put, and keep, everyone you need in your pocket. That's the nice thing about having a &quot;currency&quot; that regenerates more slowly than, say, Essence in Exalted: being out of, or low on, legend and willpower can make things significantly difficult for you. Sure, some knacks don't cost Legend to activate, but many do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to regenerate Legend, just head down to the prison basketball court and stunt like crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:31:28-08:00","id":21971,"title":"","content":"Until you run out of epic ways to describe your character doing things with a basketball. I just don't think the legendnomics works out, that your legend income by stunting will let you mindbend a large number of people simultaneously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:38:49-08:00","id":22004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21971#post21971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until you run out of epic ways to describe your character doing things with a basketball. I just don't think the legendnomics works out, that your legend income by stunting will let you mindbend a large number of people simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that predominantly non-white prison populations aren't going to contribute a whole lot to a white Scion's Legend, particularly if it involves making them look like a bunch of amateurs on the basketball court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T18:31:10-08:00","id":22043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=21366#post21366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the correct response to, say, Jormungdar rampaging through Scandinavia is to call in a barrage of ICBMs or tactical nuclear munitions, I feel that Scion has lost something of its focus on mythology and epic adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuclear Strikes are not Epic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=26YLehuMydo\" data-code=\"26YLehuMydo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/26YLehuMydo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Not one bit...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T21:32:06-08:00","id":22109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22043#post22043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuclear Strikes are not Epic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=26YLehuMydo\" data-code=\"26YLehuMydo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/26YLehuMydo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Not one bit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Epic <i>adventure</i> is the quote. It may be an epic event (at least for the more recently created meanings of epic, anyway), and something genuinely terrible and awesome to see, but &quot;the military drops a few nukes while the mythological heroes twiddle their thumbs&quot; does not make a particularly great adventure for said heroes.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> As an aside, while I even like the idea that humanity has created a weapon so powerful it is a something of a threat even to gods, I feel like people tend to give nukes too much credit (anyone familiar with the gun arguments in Exalted? Kinda like that in a larger scale) something as terrible as Typhon should be much more dangerous. Ultimate powers in particular should be capable of things that make nukes not seem like a big deal.<br /> <br /> Take the natural world into consideration:<br /> <br /> - During its life cycle an average hurricane can expend as much energy as about 10,000 nuclear bombs.<br /> <br /> - To get about the same energy released in a (luckily for the continued existence of human life) incredibly rare mega-colossal eruption of a class 8 volcano, it would require the USA and Russia to use their entire estimated nuclear arsenal simultaneously.<br /> <br /> - Likewise, the tectonic forces behind tsunamis and earthquakes can also make a nuke seem pathetic (though earthquakes are often less directly destructive than nukes, due to the energy being released over a truly colossal area, only a small fraction of which is the surface where human civilization exists).<br /> <br /> It is also part of the whole myth angle. It should not be possible to beat a magical serpent big enough to <i>encircle the world</i> with a nuke, much less a hammer, but Thor can do it due to his divine might. A lot of feats of divine beings are inconsistent and often make little sense if you try to get the math to work. No wonder some gods end up as comic book characters. Inconsistent depiction of powers has a long historical tradition XD<br /> <br /> So, if you <i>really</i> want to defeat some of the worst mythological threats via nuke, you don't go to the military. You get a Scion who developed a new Atomic Purview to do the job =D<br /> <br /> (sorry if this whole post seems disjointed or inconsistent. It is past 3 AM where I live)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T05:57:29-08:00","id":22295,"title":"","content":"Your post makes a good deal of sense.<br /> <br /> I'm again reminded of the supernatural weaponry the Hindu Pantheon are supposed to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:27:39-08:00","id":22411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22109#post22109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Epic <i>adventure</i> is the quote. It may be an epic event (at least for the more recently created meanings of epic, anyway), and something genuinely terrible and awesome to see, but &quot;the military drops a few nukes while the mythological heroes twiddle their thumbs&quot; does not make a particularly great adventure for said heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But that has nothing to the weapon itself and everything to do with the heroes twiddling their thumbs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, while I even like the idea that humanity has created a weapon so powerful it is a something of a threat even to gods, I feel like people tend to give nukes too much credit (anyone familiar with the gun arguments in Exalted? Kinda like that in a larger scale) </div> </div> </div> Was there ever a time in human history where people believed that the proliferation of firearms would bring about <i>the end of all civilization</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:45:07-08:00","id":22426,"title":"","content":"Yes. There was such a time. The idea that peasants could arm themselves with weapons that required no training to use and could kill any man, even a well-armed, well-armored, battle-hardened warrior? It was <i>absolutely terrifying</i> and did indeed result in several civilizations simply vanishing as they were unable to deal with the changes that resulted. Others were overwhelmed by the incredible power of firearms vs traditional weapons and conquered. I really hope that wasn't a serious question.<br /> <br /> Exalted and Scion are very focused on individual heroes being way cooler, more amazing, more badass and more epic (in the literal sense) than armies. Armies are scenery for your heroes to fight against. Individuals are what matter and if you bring in nukes, ICBMs and all that other annoying realistically-dangerous stuff, it makes the individual actions of the heroes far less central.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:28:17-08:00","id":22592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22426#post22426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. There was such a time. The idea that peasants could arm themselves with weapons that required no training to use and could kill any man, even a well-armed, well-armored, battle-hardened warrior? It was <i>absolutely terrifying</i> and did indeed result in several civilizations simply vanishing as they were unable to deal with the changes that resulted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Civilizations ended. But I'm not talking about one. Not talking about multiple or several. <u>All</u> Civilization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted and Scion are very focused on individual heroes being way cooler, more amazing, more badass and more epic (in the literal sense) than armies. </div> </div> </div>Unless said armies are made up of heroes. In which case, Individuals get <i>wrecked </i>fucking hard. Y'know, as it happened in the Usurpation in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Though that's a different game entirely.<br /> <br /> But enough of this disgression, point is, if you can tell an epic tale during a Siege or in the wake of a natural (or supernatural) disaster, you can tell one during Nuclear strike. I mean really, what is an ICBM if not a modern take on Fire and Brimstone raining down from the sky?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:53:15-08:00","id":22612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22592#post22592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Civilizations ended. But I'm not talking about one. Not talking about multiple or several. <u>All</u> Civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could walk two blocks to my local protest group, who would happily suggest that <u>All</u> civilization is going to end because of abortion / stem cells / gay marriage / obama / general sin / some other hot topic. People believe a lot of things, in very large numbers, that I suspect may not be true.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But enough of this disgression, point is, if you can tell an epic tale during a Siege or in the wake of a natural (or supernatural) disaster, you can tell one during Nuclear strike. I mean really, what is an ICBM if not a modern take on Fire and Brimstone raining down from the sky? </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. It is completely possible to tell an amazing story in a homebrew setting based on the threat of nuclear apocalypse, the immediate reality of nuclear apocalypse, or following a nuclear apocalypse. I have personally played in and run games based around such settings for Scion and had enormous fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:58:58-08:00","id":22618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22592#post22592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But enough of this disgression, point is, if you can tell an epic tale during a Siege or in the wake of a natural (or supernatural) disaster, you can tell one during Nuclear strike. I mean really, what is an ICBM if not a modern take on Fire and Brimstone raining down from the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Stories that become epic sagas can be built around anything. I've seen campaigns built around global plague, nuclear fallout, and one even started using a Second Great Depression as a setting point. It's really up to the STs and their groups to make things epic, even if that means a nuclear strike is involved. Or mortals. Or, I dunno, sea-monkies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T16:07:00-08:00","id":22679,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* A nuke would clear the mortals out fairly well. Radiation sickness...and no foodstuffs, etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T17:09:42-08:00","id":22731,"title":"","content":"My point isn't that it's <i>impossible</i> to tell great stories using the idea that human weapons can and do threaten the Divine. My point is that such stories are fairly niche and the basic premise of Scion, as I understand it and believe it should be, is that Legendary Beings are amazing heroes and individually shape the destiny of the world. The focus should be on them, and mortal weapons should be scenery. It's basically the inverse ninja law, with humans being the ninjas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T17:13:23-08:00","id":22737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22731#post22731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's basically the inverse ninja law, with humans being the ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how having more humans on stage means they should be less effective individually at all curtails the probability of mortal entanglements.<br /> <br /> If you don't want mortals to matter in your games, that's fine. There's no reason to strenuously object to the idea that they could matter if the person running a particular chronicle wanted them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T00:31:13-08:00","id":22997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22731#post22731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point isn't that it's <i>impossible</i> to tell great stories using the idea that human weapons can and do threaten the Divine. My point is that such stories are fairly niche and the basic premise of Scion, as I understand it and believe it should be, is that Legendary Beings are amazing heroes and individually shape the destiny of the world. The focus should be on them, and mortal weapons should be scenery. It's basically the inverse ninja law, with humans being the ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Telgar, it is not impossible. I do understand that you believe that &quot;if mortals can threaten the divine, then they are not so divine after all&quot; but you have to think of the inverse &quot;if the divine can be threatened, then that does make them scared&quot; and that fear can bring about amazing stories in and of itself. Some of the divine can work with mortals to bring about an end to the Titan war. Others may seek to send out tendrils and take control of mortal institutions. Still others may seek to just wipe the mortals off the planet. While others may seek to take them back to the stone age.<br /> <br /> It is not impossible as you suggested. In fact, it makes for a far more interesting campaign if the mortals -can- threaten the divine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T01:17:48-08:00","id":23011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19994-mortal-antagonists?p=22997#post22997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not impossible as you suggested. In fact, it makes for a far more interesting campaign if the mortals -can- threaten the divine.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't say it was impossible. He said it isn't impossible. He just said it in a way that almost sounds like a double negative. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T03:02:34-08:00","id":23036,"title":"","content":"My bad, then. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:48:01-08:00","id":23111,"title":"","content":"It's like a knight fighting a dragon. It makes a good story when the knight wins. But no one will bet against the dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T16:00:21-08:00","id":23365,"title":"","content":"St. George says Lolno.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.illusionsgallery.com/St-George-L.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> All right, take a look at that fucking Dragon. Small, Pathetic, barely comes up to Georgie's Horse, I owned DOGS bigger and tougher than this dragon.<br /> Which is the point of the legend of St. George, one of the OG &quot;Knight vs Dragon&quot; tales.<br /> <br /> Basically, back in the day it wasn't a matter of it being cool if the Knight (Good) defeated the Dragon (Evil) it was that, Good must always be stronger than Evil. The point of that entire legend is &quot;Always bet on the Knight. Because the Dragon is a <i>fucking sissy</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"